ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{x})+\\frac{2}{x} \\\\  & =x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})+\\frac{2}{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{2}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535938 true] [17592186375307 1017 #edb/ref 17592186375308 13194139535938 true] [17592186375307 1089 "q-130082" 13194139535938 true] [17592186375307 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535938 true] [17592186375307 1100 "Given that $D=x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y={x}^{2}-2x?$" 13194139535938 true] [17592186375307 1113 #uuid "8616e65f-08e1-5256-9739-a39cfbef8685" 13194139535938 true] [17592186375307 1145 "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}=x,{f}_{1}=1,$ and ${f}_{0}=0.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D({x}^{2}-2x) \\\\  & =(x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x})({x}^{2}-2x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({x}^{2}-2x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}-2x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x-2)+(2x-2) \\\\  & =2x+2x-2 \\\\  & =4x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535938 true] [17592186375308 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375309 13194139535938 true] [17592186375308 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375310 13194139535938 true] [17592186375308 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375311 13194139535938 true] [17592186375308 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375312 13194139535938 true] [17592186375308 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375313 13194139535938 true] [17592186375308 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535938 true] [17592186375308 1041 "selection" 13194139535938 true] [17592186375308 1104 #edb/ref 17592186375311 13194139535938 true] [17592186375308 1110 #uuid "5838ff18-dac6-5a7e-ae4c-a12d2862eec6" 13194139535938 true] [17592186375